WEBVTT

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:02.980
Wendy, they're dead!

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:03.990
Brody, pull it together.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.580
We don't have a chance, okay?

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.980
We have to get out of here now!

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.560
No, Brody.We are not leaving.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.210
We have got to find my sister.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:10.950
No!

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.800
No, I am getting out of here right now!

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:13.740
Brody!

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.220
Brody, get back here!

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.640
Brody!

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.070
God, you son of a bitch!

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.620
Cut.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.540
What the hell was that?

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:48.470
Thanks.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.460
Here you go.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.730
Thanks, Walter.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.230
Don't mark that.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.290
It's all good, Tara.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:01:59.750
That was great.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:00.940
Uh, let's do it again.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.630
Uh, maybe we try dialing
up that scream, huh?

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.540
I know, I know.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.810
I'm just -- I'm having
trouble with the tennis ball.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.060
That is just for cg registration.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.870
When ivan and the fx guys are done,
it is going to look terrifying.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.630
You want to look at the
concept sketches again?

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.660
No, that's okay.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.530
I'll find it.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.100
I know you will, pumpkin, huh?

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:20.990
Okay.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.350
Going again, everybody.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.980
10-Minute reload for camera and sound.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.130
No, man, I'm telling you.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:33.530
Working alone behind the sets or after
wrap, I catch this weird vibe sometimes.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.020
Like what?

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.990
Mmm, like something's watching.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:38.980
Come on.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.230
Hey.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.930
Working on a movie like this?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.070
Weird crap's bound to happen.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:47.680
Frank thinks the stage is
haunted. Like, for real.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:53.840
All I'm saying is, they call wrap,
I get done, and I get out of here.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.360
Fast.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.370
Guy is definitely off his meds.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.560
Brody, come back.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.020
You son of a bitch.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:22.660
Brody, come back, you son of a bitch.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:28.900
Hello?

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.190
Guys?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:42.580
Come on.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.580
It's not funny.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.670
Okay.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:48.810
Ha ha, very funny.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.570
Hello?

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.280
Who's there?

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.740
Now, that's what I'm talking about!

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:43.260
First opened in 1927, the lot has been
in continuous operation for eight decades.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.810
Hey, you know this is where
they filmed "Creepshow"?

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:50.540
Now to the right here is Stars Hollow.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.390
It's the setting for the
television series "Gilmore Girls."

00:04:55.390 --> 00:05:01.020
And if we're lucky, we might even
catch one of the show's stars.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.470
Come on.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.150
Let's finish the tour.

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:11.040
And then up to the right here, we have New York
Avenue, and that's where they shot "Lois & Clark."

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:16.480
Sammy, check it out.

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:18.090
It's matt damon.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:19.430
Yeah.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.730
I'm pretty sure that's not Matt Damon.

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.590
No, it is.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:24.550
Well, Matt Damon just picked
up a broom and started sweeping.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.700
Yeah, he was probably
researching a role or something.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.840
Uh, I don't think so.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.110
Hey, this way.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.180
Uh, I think stage 9's over here.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:32.780
Come on, man.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:33.770
Let's keep going this way.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:34.500
No, come on.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:35.260
We got to work.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:35.950
Golly.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.140
Dude, you wanted to come to L.A.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.340
Yeah, for a vacation!

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.710
I mean, swimming pools and movie stars!

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.770
Not to work.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:44.290
This seem like swimming
pool weather to you, Dean?

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.760
It's practically canadian.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.030
Yeah.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:52.720
I just figured that, you know, after everything that happened
with madison, you could use a little R&R,  that's all.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:53.790
Maybe I want to work, Dean.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.090
Maybe it keeps my mind off things.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:57.000
Okay, okay, all right.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.830
So this crew guy, what,
did he ...he died on set?

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:03.160
Yeah, rumors spreading
like wildfire online.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.270
They're saying the set's haunted.

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:06.820
Like "poltergeist"?

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.160
Could be a poltergeist.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:08.730
No, no, no.

00:06:08.730 --> 00:06:10.420
The movie "poltergeist."

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:12.910
You know nothing of your
cultural heritage, do you?

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:20.010
It was rumored that the set of "poltergeist" was
cursed, that they used real human bones as props.

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:22.600
Like, at least three of
the actors died in it.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.810
Yeah, might be something like that.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:26.740
All right, so this crew guy.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.680
What's his name?

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.930
Frank Jaffe.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.080
You got a death certificate
or a coroner's report?

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.920
Well, no, but, uh, it's L.A., You know?

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.340
That might not even be his real name.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:39.120
But the girl who found him, she said
she saw something ... a vanishing figure.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.120
What's the girl's name?

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.080
Uh, Tara Benchley.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.260
Whoa, Tara Benchley?

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:46.260
From "feardotcom" and
"ghost ship" Tara Benchley?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.100
Dude, why didn't you say so?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.440
So now you're suddenly on board?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.110
I mean, I'm a fan of her work.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.490
It's very good.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:06:59.790
No, look.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:00.510
Don't get me wrong.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:03.420
Everyone at this studio loves
the dailies, myself included.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.990
We were just wondering if it could be...

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:07.850
You know, a little brighter.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:09.470
Brighter?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.650
Yeah, Jay, more color.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:12.790
Mcg, you know what I'm saying.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.140
You're the master of that stuff.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:15.880
Brad, this is a horror movie.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.550
Who says horror has to be dark?

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.720
It's just -- It's sort of
depressing, don't you think?

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:21.650
Uh, excuse me.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.530
Uh, green-Shirt guy?

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:25.110
Yeah, yeah, you.Come here.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:30.140
Can you get me a, uh,
smoothie from craft?

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.060
You want a what from who?

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.250
You are a P.A.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.560
This is what you do.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.540
Yeah, he, uh...

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:42.030
One smoothie coming right up.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:46.530
What's a P.A.?

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:48.580
I think they're kind of like slaves.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.100
They'll let anybody
in this business, huh?

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.190
6, 6, 6. Mark.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:34.620
Ready!

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.500
Okay, why don't we take it
from, "come on, it'll be fun"?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.720
And action.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.280
Come on.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:40.660
It'll be fun.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.590
Dicta sunt explicabo.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.000
God, I hate you so much right now.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.180
Cut!

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:20.360
Very nice.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:22.930
So?

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:24.710
No emf anywhere.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.400
Great.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.190
So, what do you think?

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:29.200
Well, I think being a P.A.Sucks, but...

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.220
But the food these people get?

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:31.840
Are you kidding me?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.260
I mean, look at these things.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.490
They're like miniature
philly cheesesteak sandwiches.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:37.940
They're delicious.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.420
Maybe later.

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.060
What did you find out
about the dead crew guy?

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.030
Uh, Frank Jaffe was just
filling in for the day.

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:53.370
Nobody here knew him or
where he lived or anything.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:53.950
Oh, great.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:55.200
So you found out about as much as I did.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.120
Hey, guys.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.170
Oh, hey.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.630
They're wonderful.

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:00.680
Listen.

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.850
I did dig up some stuff
about stage 9's history.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:08.260
Four people died messy here over the past 80
years, two suicides and two fatal accidents.

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:09.890
Any one of those could
be a vengeful spirit.

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:11.220
Yeah.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:13.100
Just got to narrow it down more.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.150
I'll get right on that.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:33.260
Hey, are you supposed
to get one of these?

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.920
I..I don't really know what I'm doing.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.060
First day?

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:44.980
Yeah, my big break.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.550
You know, I know it's really uncool
to say this, but I'm a big fan.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:52.750
I loved you in "boogeyman."

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:53.730
Oh, god.

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:55.760
What a terrible script.

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.100
Uh, but, thank you.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.610
Yeah.

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.590
You found him, right?

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.850
The -- The
dead guy?

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.330
I'm sorry.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.720
You probably don't
want to talk about this.

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:13.190
No, no, actually,
it's -- It's okay.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.660
Nobody around here really
brings it up very much.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.120
I think they're all scared I'm
gonna have some kind of breakdown.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.020
That must have been awful.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.310
What happened?

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:28.100
It was horrible.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:35.730
There ... there was all this blood coming
from his eyes, from his mouth, and, uh...

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.990
I saw this, um...

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:42.830
What?

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:48.010
I saw this shape.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:51.970
To tell you the truth, I
don't know actually what I saw.

00:11:51.970 --> 00:11:53.770
I just know I saw it.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:55.830
Thanks, Walter.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.940
Uh, so this -- This crew
guy Frank, did you know him?

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.140
No, not that well.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:05.730
That's funny.

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.200
It's like no one around
here actually knew the guy.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:09.480
I got his picture.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:11.360
You do?

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.150
Yeah.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:14.510
I take polaroids of all the crew.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:17.200
It's just one of those things
you do to kill time on the set.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:22.490
Right there.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.830
Son of a bitch.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:38.210
Gerard st.James?

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.480
Yes?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.310
You're still alive, and
you're not Frank Jaffe.

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:43.510
NO

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:48.180
You were -- You were desert soldier number 4
in "Metalstorm: The destruction of jared-Syn."

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.060
I was.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:50.770
I knew I recognized you.

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:52.670
I am a huge fan.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:57.620
I mean, your turn as the tractor-Crash
victim in "Critters 3" ...wow.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:59.570
Hey, well, please.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.340
Come in.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:10.270
Thanks.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:11.470
Yeah, it was the producers.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:13.610
I mean, they brought me in
for the day to play Frank.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:15.760
Just to fake your death?

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:18.270
Well, rumors of a haunted film set...

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:24.880
Free publicity, especially when you're making a horror
movie I mean, it's already all over the internet.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.500
Yeah, we know.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:31.050
These days, it's all about
new media, building buzz.

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:34.250
They say I'm the new "lonelygirl."

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:35.840
Who?

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:37.760
And the ghost Tara saw?

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:40.280
Projected on a screen of diffusion.

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.990
Isn't that kind of cruel...

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:44.380
Messing with their heads like that?

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.390
Hey, I just play the part.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:48.040
I don't write the script.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:50.010
Speaking of...

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:56.470
I'm playing willy in a dinner-Theater production
of "salesman" at costa mesa all next month.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:59.430
Get a free pepper steak with the coupon.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.180
Well, now, wait a second.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:03.510
If you're seen in public,
won't that ruin the hoax?

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.750
Oh, please.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:08.410
Frank and willy, , ,
totally different characters.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:09.760
You know what?

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:11.760
Thanks very much, Mr. Saint.James.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:12.750
It was just nagging at us.

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:17.820
But we're ...we're very glad,
you know, you're alive and well.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.160
Yeah.

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.290
Absolutely.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.320
I wanted to ask you.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.810
What was it like working
with Richard Moll?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:31.850
He's from "metalstorm."

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:35.110
He was Hurok, King
of the Cyclops people.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.010
Gentleman's gentleman.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.380
Yeah?

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:41.620
All right.

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:43.100
Pepper steak.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.340
When we read from that book, we must
have brought them back...back from hell.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:53.490
Now they're trying to use us...

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:54.880
It doesn't matter.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:57.030
We're not going till we
find Wendy and her sister.

00:14:57.030 --> 00:14:58.380
Got it?

00:14:58.380 --> 00:14:59.300
Good.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:00.910
Now, let's get busy.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:03.690
Cut!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:04.550
No good for sound.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:06.490
I'm getting some kind of feedback.

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.160
Another costly sound delay.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.060
All right, we're going
again for sound, people!

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:14.520
Thank you!

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:17.930
No, it's a great scene,
really ..Dynamite.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.080
But I still got a few...

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.330
Not -- Not problems,
just questions.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.670
Like what?

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:28.280
Well, for one thing. The rules
aren't really landing for me.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:33.570
Like, the kids do this latin chant,
and that makes the ghosts show up?

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.660
Yeah.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.670
If the ghosts are in hell,
how do they hear the chanting?

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:40.580
I mean, what, do they
have super hearing?

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:41.680
Well, it's a logic bump.

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:43.310
The rules don't track.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:46.080
Marty, you're the writer.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.690
What about throwing in an explainer?

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:48.450
Yeah, that'd be super.

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:50.070
I got to check some messages.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:54.690
Suits.

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:13.260
Has mcg seen this?

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:18.340
I like the whole body-Paint,
black-And-White thing, but, gee, I...

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:22.460
I don't think those neck wounds
are really gonna read on-Camera.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.770
They need to be red.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:26.470
You know what I'm saying?

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:27.650
Hey, Jay!

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.640
I need to speak to makeup.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:33.340
Yeah?

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.460
Wait up.

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:59.050
When we read from that book, we must
have brought them back ...back from hell.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:00.260
I don't understand.

00:17:00.260 --> 00:17:02.450
If they were in hell, how
could they hear our chanting?

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.380
They must have super hearing.

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:39.140
Wendy?

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:39.980
Oh, Mitch!

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:41.230
God, you're alive!

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:43.000
You won't get rid of me that easy.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.250
Rumble, rumble, rumble!

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:47.270
Salt.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:48.250
Okay, we need salt.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:51.440
I read in that book that
it keeps ghosts away.

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:54.390
Kendra, logan, you guys check the back.

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:57.680
The poor bastard killed
himself, like, for real.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.390
Shouldn't we shut it down or something?

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.030
We had a moment of silence
for him at breakfast.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.820
He was just a studio guy.

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:05.230
Shh.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.350
I love you.

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:07.260
I know.

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:10.170
I'm sorry.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:14.840
Can we ...can we cut or something?

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:17.200
Uh, yeah.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:17.600
Cut.

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:18.380
Cut!

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.570
That's a cut!

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:24.400
Only I get to say "cut."

00:18:25.820 --> 00:18:27.340
Hey, what's up?

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:29.200
I'm just a little upset.

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:32.850
With everything that's been
going on, who can blame you?

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:35.750
I just can't wrap my head
around the dialogue, you know?

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.970
"Salt" -- Doesn't
that sound silly?

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.480
I mean, why would a
ghost be afraid of salt?

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:42.100
Okay, um...

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.710
Marty, what do you think?

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:46.220
Not married to salt.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:46.770
What do you want?

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:48.580
We still sticking with condiments?

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:51.540
Mmm, it just sounds
different, not better.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:53.120
What else would a ghost be scared of?

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:54.880
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:57.400
What would a ghost be scared of?

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:59.160
Maybe shotguns.

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:02.620
That makes even less sense than salt.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.370
These people are idiots.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:11.280
Walter's a little testy for a P.A., Huh?

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.510
How's it going in here?

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:17.930
Really good -- Tara has stepped up her performance,
and I think it's from the sense-Memory stuff.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:18.770
Sense-Memory?

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:19.890
Yeah.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.730
Dean, you know, when I ask how it's going
here, I'm talking about the case, right?

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.330
We don't really work here.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:28.240
You know, I thought
you hated being a P.A.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:31.990
I don't know.

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:32.730
It's not so bad.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.590
I kind of feel like part
of the team, you know?

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:35.420
It's good.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.530
Oh, taquito?

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:37.700
They're wonderful.

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:38.530
No.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.460
Um, listen.

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:42.030
I conned my way into the morgue.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.990
News reports are right.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.640
Brad's a doornail
-- No question.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:46.670
Copy that.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:47.410
Sorry.What?

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:48.270
"Copy that"?

00:19:48.270 --> 00:19:49.040
What did you say?

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:50.170
The news reports are right.

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:51.010
Brad's a doornail.

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:51.920
They're aware.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:52.840
Who's aware?

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:53.520
Sorry.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.460
What were you saying?

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:57.440
Uh, uh, the newspaper's right.

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:58.390
Brad's a doornail.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:19:59.330
No question about it.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:01.090
I guess it's a good
thing we didn't skip town.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:02.070
Oh, come here.

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.510
I want you to hear something.

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:04.430
Copy that.

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:05.710
On my way.

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:08.480
Hey, Dave.

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.540
Can you play that thing
you were playing me earlier?

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.910
Sure.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.720
Thanks.

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.540
It doesn't matter.

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.840
We're not leaving till we
find Wendy and her sister.

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:22.090
Got it?

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:23.240
Good.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.930
Now, let's get busy.

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.170
E.V.P.

00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.880
From the night of Brad's stage dive.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:34.030
All of a sudden, I'm getting
electromagnetic readings up the wazoo.

00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:36.210
For some reason, it's
a legit haunting now.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:36.980
Well, whose ghost, Dean?

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:37.710
What's it want?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:40.300
I think we should take a
look at Brad's death scene.

00:21:02.230 --> 00:21:03.550
Now, where'd you get this dvd?

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:05.090
They're called dailies.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:06.270
I got it from cindy.

00:21:06.270 --> 00:21:08.480
She's kind of got this
thing going with drew.

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.220
He dubbed me an extra copy.

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:13.950
All right.

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:15.650
Here's where the guy
fell through the roof.

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.170
Right.

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:20.140
All right, here we go.

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.940
They must have super hearing.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:26.400
Wait.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:27.710
Go back, go back.

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.870
Right after -- Right
after -- Yeah, right.

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:32.940
Wait.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.300
There.

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:41.160
It's like "3 men and
a baby" all over again.

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:47.260
Selleck, danson, and guttenberg,
and I don't know who played the baby.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:48.390
What's your point?

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.980
There's a scene where people say that
the camera caught a ghost on film.

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:55.210
Apparently, in the background of one of the
scenes, there was this boy that nobody remembers.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.130
Spirit photography.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:02.830
I've seen her before.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:09.960
Here.Check this out.

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:13.370
Yeah, go for ozzie.

00:22:15.610 --> 00:22:17.170
No, I don't have a 20 on Tara.

00:22:17.170 --> 00:22:18.160
I think she's 10-100.

00:22:20.300 --> 00:22:21.800
Okay, copy that.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:23.130
I'm sorry.

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:24.520
What were you saying?

00:22:26.970 --> 00:22:30.370
Elise Drummond. Starlet
back in the '30s.

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:35.870
Had an affair with a studio exec.

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:38.410
He uses her up, fires
her, leaves her destitute.

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:42.410
Elise hangs herself from stage 9's rafters
right into a scene they're shooting.

00:22:42.410 --> 00:22:43.900
Just like our man Brad.

00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:45.840
So, what, she's got it
in for the studio brass?

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:46.970
Possibly.

00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:50.420
I mean, it's a motive, and
Brad's death matches hers exactly.

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:52.490
We're digging tonight, aren't we?

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:55.090
That's a wrap, people!

00:22:55.090 --> 00:22:58.170
6:00 A.M.Call for crew tomorrow.

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:01.390
Great work, everybody!

00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:04.640
Mcg, you're a genius.

00:23:04.640 --> 00:23:07.080
You're kickin' ass and taking names.

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:08.330
Good night, Jay.

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:10.400
Yeah.

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:14.410
Which way?

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:16.990
Over here.

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:23.730
Hey.

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:24.880
Yeah?

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:29.610
Hey, this map is totally
worth the 5 bucks.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:33.010
Hey, we got to go check out Johnny
Ramone's grave when we're done here.

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:34.720
You want to dig him up, too?

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:37.080
Bite your tongue, heathen!

00:23:37.080 --> 00:23:40.070
You know, Dean, what I
don't get is, why now?

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:43.800
I mean, after 75 years, Elise
Drummond suddenly goes homicidal.

00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:44.910
You know, why this movie?

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:47.110
Well, maybe she's mad they're
making a scary ghost flick.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:48.500
Is it really that scary?

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:49.550
Here we go.

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:54.700
Yahtzee.

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:06.140
I know.

00:24:06.140 --> 00:24:09.330
No, I friggin' hate mcg's dailies.

00:24:09.330 --> 00:24:10.690
I can't control the guy.

00:24:10.690 --> 00:24:13.970
I'm telling you -- Next
one I'm directing myself.

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:15.910
What, you?

00:24:15.910 --> 00:24:17.010
No, bob.

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:18.200
You I love.

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:19.180
You're a genius.

00:24:19.180 --> 00:24:21.490
You're kicking ass and taking names.

00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:23.060
Yeah, okay.

00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:24.080
Yeah.

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:25.130
Talk to you later, babe.

00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:26.410
Uh-Huh.

00:24:26.910 --> 00:24:28.280
What a dick.

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:31.240
Oh, great.

00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:35.660
Hey, guys!

00:24:36.020 --> 00:24:37.620
Producer walking here!

00:24:37.620 --> 00:24:39.350
Hello!

00:25:36.870 --> 00:25:37.870
Hey!

00:25:40.050 --> 00:25:41.080
Hey, pal.

00:25:41.120 --> 00:25:43.190
Can you, uh, show me to the exit?

00:25:43.190 --> 00:25:45.400
I can't see a damn thing here.

00:25:49.630 --> 00:25:50.890
Hey!

00:25:51.310 --> 00:25:52.170
Hey, putz.

00:25:52.170 --> 00:25:53.550
I'm talking to you.

00:25:53.610 --> 00:25:55.330
Somebody could get hurt here.

00:26:02.890 --> 00:26:04.310
What the hell?

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:15.960
No!

00:26:20.300 --> 00:26:21.850
No!

00:26:50.230 --> 00:26:52.130
They never forgive.

00:26:53.330 --> 00:26:55.410
They never forget.

00:26:55.430 --> 00:26:56.650
Mitch?

00:26:57.160 --> 00:26:57.940
Ashley?

00:26:57.940 --> 00:27:01.850
This summer, they're coming
back again to settle the score...

00:27:01.850 --> 00:27:03.350
Again.

00:27:03.850 --> 00:27:05.290
You out here?

00:27:08.480 --> 00:27:09.910
Ashley and Todd
-- They're dead!

00:27:09.910 --> 00:27:11.060
Wendy, they're dead!

00:27:11.060 --> 00:27:13.640
These bastards aren't taking
us, not without a fight.

00:27:13.640 --> 00:27:15.150
I am getting out of here right now!

00:27:15.150 --> 00:27:16.340
Brody!

00:27:16.770 --> 00:27:19.080
From the makers of
"Cornfield Massacre"...

00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:22.300
"Monster truck, " "Charlie's angels"...

00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:23.760
"Charlie's Angels 2: Full throttle"...

00:27:23.760 --> 00:27:28.190
And "Hell hazers" comes a
new experience in terror.

00:27:29.130 --> 00:27:33.050
<i>We must have brought them
back ...back from hell. AGAIN</i>

00:27:36.560 --> 00:27:38.090
<i>This film not yet rated</i>

00:27:39.930 --> 00:27:41.970
Rolled in with a giant fan.

00:27:41.970 --> 00:27:45.990
Same thing happened to an electrician
back in '66 -- A guy named Billy Beard.

00:27:45.990 --> 00:27:47.320
What the hell, dude?

00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:47.960
I don't know.

00:27:47.960 --> 00:27:50.430
It doesn't seem like Elise this time.

00:27:50.430 --> 00:27:51.240
We already torched her.

00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:52.390
Are we dealing with another ghost?

00:27:52.390 --> 00:27:53.060
Maybe.

00:27:53.060 --> 00:27:55.050
Yeah, but these things
don't usually tag-Team.

00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:00.210
Everybody!

00:28:00.220 --> 00:28:01.800
Gather around, okay?

00:28:01.800 --> 00:28:03.390
I got an announcement to make.

00:28:03.540 --> 00:28:04.910
Hold that for me.

00:28:06.990 --> 00:28:08.020
Everyone!

00:28:08.490 --> 00:28:09.430
Huddle in!

00:28:12.570 --> 00:28:21.880
In light of Jay's accident last night and in cooperation with
the authorities, we're shutting down production for a few days.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:24.000
I know, I know.

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:25.820
Look, I'm not going to lie to you.

00:28:25.820 --> 00:28:28.430
We've had a few setbacks this week.

00:28:28.430 --> 00:28:32.750
But we all know what Jay and
Brad wanted more than anything.

00:28:33.810 --> 00:28:39.380
And that was to see "Hell Hazers 2: The
Reckoning" on screens all across America.

00:28:39.660 --> 00:28:46.230
Now, we owe it to them to go on and to
pull together and make this damn movie, huh?

00:28:47.600 --> 00:28:50.600
But... but ... but ... but
...but not ... not today.

00:28:50.600 --> 00:28:52.330
Go home.

00:28:52.330 --> 00:28:54.090
Someone will call you.

00:28:58.240 --> 00:28:59.360
Wendy.

00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:01.740
What, are you afraid of ghosts?

00:29:01.740 --> 00:29:02.470
Come on.

00:29:02.470 --> 00:29:04.070
It'll be fun.

00:29:07.720 --> 00:29:08.940
Hey.

00:29:08.940 --> 00:29:10.160
Hey.

00:29:10.970 --> 00:29:13.540
So, you find out where
the electrician's buried?

00:29:13.540 --> 00:29:14.940
He wasn't.

00:29:14.940 --> 00:29:16.600
Billy beard was cremated.

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:18.500
Great.

00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:19.940
Now what?

00:29:19.940 --> 00:29:21.280
No idea.

00:29:21.400 --> 00:29:23.660
Anymore ghost cameos in the dailies?

00:29:23.660 --> 00:29:26.090
Not in the first six hours.

00:29:27.270 --> 00:29:27.960
You know.

00:29:27.960 --> 00:29:32.110
Maybe the spirits are trying to shut
down the movie 'cause they think it sucks.

00:29:32.110 --> 00:29:33.640
'Cause, I mean, it kind of does.

00:29:33.640 --> 00:29:36.300
From, uh, "come on, it'll be fun"?

00:29:36.300 --> 00:29:37.090
Come on.

00:29:37.090 --> 00:29:38.450
It'll be fun.

00:29:52.590 --> 00:29:56.600
Listen to the invocation.

00:29:56.600 --> 00:30:01.310
Dean, that's the real deal a
necromantic summoning ritual.

00:30:04.430 --> 00:30:07.100
What the hell is that
doing in a hollywood movie?

00:30:07.100 --> 00:30:07.550
No, dear.

00:30:07.550 --> 00:30:08.830
We're down for a few days.

00:30:08.830 --> 00:30:13.490
It's cool, it gives me time to
pitch that time-Travel thing.

00:30:13.840 --> 00:30:14.690
Yeah.

00:30:14.730 --> 00:30:15.300
All right, well, look.

00:30:15.300 --> 00:30:16.320
Get back to me on this, all right?

00:30:16.320 --> 00:30:17.180
Seriously.

00:30:17.180 --> 00:30:18.920
No, I'm serious.

00:30:18.920 --> 00:30:20.020
Dude, are you serious?

00:30:20.020 --> 00:30:21.420
'Cause I'm serious.

00:30:21.420 --> 00:30:22.590
All right.

00:30:22.590 --> 00:30:23.710
Cool.

00:30:24.010 --> 00:30:24.930
Guys, we're all shut down.

00:30:24.930 --> 00:30:26.070
What are you still doing here?

00:30:26.070 --> 00:30:27.660
Yeah, uh...

00:30:27.660 --> 00:30:29.580
Really sorry, man.

00:30:29.580 --> 00:30:32.040
We -- We -- We
couldn't help ourselves.

00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:34.840
We just had to tell you
that we read the script.

00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:35.910
And?

00:30:36.830 --> 00:30:38.100
Yeah.

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.400
It's, uh...

00:30:40.400 --> 00:30:41.300
It's awesome.

00:30:41.300 --> 00:30:42.500
Awesome.

00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:43.640
Really awesome.

00:30:43.640 --> 00:30:44.050
I know.

00:30:44.050 --> 00:30:45.200
It's pretty rockin', right?

00:30:45.200 --> 00:30:46.340
I'm glad you guys liked it.

00:30:46.340 --> 00:30:46.940
Yeah.

00:30:46.940 --> 00:30:49.740
I-I really liked all
the attention to detail.

00:30:49.740 --> 00:30:50.250
Dude, right on.

00:30:50.250 --> 00:30:50.770
That's my thing.

00:30:50.770 --> 00:30:53.060
I mean, you know, color
me guilty, but that is me.

00:30:53.060 --> 00:30:54.830
I'm a total detail buff.

00:30:54.830 --> 00:31:00.670
No, I mean, the way you worked in all those Enochian
summoning rituals and all the authentic language and...

00:31:00.670 --> 00:31:02.750
What, you mean that latin crap?

00:31:04.930 --> 00:31:05.480
No, man.

00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:06.670
That's Walter.

00:31:06.670 --> 00:31:08.790
Walter Dixon, the original writer.

00:31:08.790 --> 00:31:10.320
You like that garbage?

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:11.880
Wait, Walter --
The P.A.Walter?

00:31:11.880 --> 00:31:12.920
No, he's not a P.A.

00:31:12.940 --> 00:31:15.860
He's got a clause in his contract
that allows him to come on set.

00:31:15.860 --> 00:31:17.410
But he wrote the invocations?

00:31:17.410 --> 00:31:19.120
He wrote a wackjob screenplay.

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:19.790
There's no pace.

00:31:19.790 --> 00:31:20.890
There's no love interest.

00:31:20.890 --> 00:31:22.390
It's all wackadoo exposition.

00:31:22.390 --> 00:31:26.570
I had to cut, like, 90% of it to make
it readable, another 10% to make it good.

00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:32.850
Should have kept
Walter's original script.

00:31:32.850 --> 00:31:34.110
It's actually pretty good.

00:31:34.110 --> 00:31:35.720
Yeah.

00:31:37.100 --> 00:31:39.770
And it reads like a how-To
manual of conjuration,

00:31:39.770 --> 00:31:43.720
Like a textbook on how to summon ghosts
and get them to do whatever you want.

00:31:43.720 --> 00:31:44.940
Yeah, like kill people.

00:31:44.950 --> 00:31:46.270
Yep.

00:31:47.480 --> 00:31:50.510
So let's say somewhere down the line,
Walter learned some pretty black magic.

00:31:50.510 --> 00:31:54.120
Yeah, and let's say he's pissed at
these people for wrecking his movie.

00:31:54.380 --> 00:31:55.500
Motive and means.

00:31:56.010 --> 00:31:57.680
It's worth checking out.

00:32:07.620 --> 00:32:08.490
So?

00:32:10.080 --> 00:32:11.190
You wanted to meet?

00:32:13.870 --> 00:32:15.300
Hey, I'm a little busy here, buddy.

00:32:15.520 --> 00:32:16.570
I'm working on a script.

00:32:16.810 --> 00:32:17.070
Oh, yeah.

00:32:17.070 --> 00:32:18.820
You guys worked on it a lot.

00:32:18.820 --> 00:32:20.360
It needed work.

00:32:20.360 --> 00:32:22.130
Now, why couldn't we have
done this in my office?

00:32:22.130 --> 00:32:27.080
You know, the history, the lore in
my draft was completely accurate.

00:32:27.080 --> 00:32:33.900
We could have gotten it right for the first time ever
in this whorehouse of a town, but you tore it to shreds.

00:32:34.650 --> 00:32:38.020
You replaced it with
cleavage and fart jokes.

00:32:39.440 --> 00:32:40.680
It was real.

00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:43.110
Who gives a rat's ass about real?

00:32:43.110 --> 00:32:44.420
We're talking about ghosts here, Walter.

00:32:44.420 --> 00:32:45.350
There's no such thing.

00:32:45.350 --> 00:32:47.380
That's where you're wrong, martin.

00:32:59.310 --> 00:33:00.560
Okay, nutjob...

00:33:00.560 --> 00:33:01.860
End of meeting.

00:33:11.570 --> 00:33:12.950
C oh, my god, no!

00:33:12.950 --> 00:33:14.500
Please, no!

00:33:14.500 --> 00:33:16.250
You ruined it, martin!

00:33:16.250 --> 00:33:17.850
Everything I worked for!

00:33:17.850 --> 00:33:20.040
Oh, god!

00:33:20.370 --> 00:33:21.080
Walter!

00:33:21.080 --> 00:33:23.660
Now you're gonna find out
what being a ghost is like!

00:33:23.660 --> 00:33:25.160
Walter, please!

00:33:25.160 --> 00:33:27.180
Walter, help me!

00:33:27.630 --> 00:33:29.030
Help!

00:33:37.950 --> 00:33:39.890
You are one hell of a P.A.

00:33:39.890 --> 00:33:41.440
Yeah, I know.

00:33:43.770 --> 00:33:45.060
What are you doing?

00:33:45.200 --> 00:33:46.930
Could ask you the same thing, Walter.

00:33:46.930 --> 00:33:48.490
Raising these spirits from the dead?

00:33:49.830 --> 00:33:50.800
Making them murder for you?

00:33:50.800 --> 00:33:52.730
That's playing with fire, Walter.

00:33:52.730 --> 00:33:54.530
You don't understand.

00:33:55.700 --> 00:33:56.070
You know what?

00:33:56.070 --> 00:33:56.550
You're right.

00:33:56.550 --> 00:33:57.950
I don't understand.

00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:01.100
Wait, look.

00:34:01.100 --> 00:34:05.710
You put your heart and soul into
something, years of hard work ... years.

00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:09.330
And then they take it,
and they crap all over it!

00:34:10.330 --> 00:34:13.550
And then -- And then they want
you to smile and say thank you.

00:34:13.550 --> 00:34:14.170
Walter, listen.

00:34:14.170 --> 00:34:15.000
It's just a movie.

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:16.170
That's it.

00:34:19.790 --> 00:34:20.660
Look.

00:34:22.690 --> 00:34:24.070
I got nothing against you, man.

00:34:24.070 --> 00:34:25.000
You're not part of this.

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:27.290
Just please --
Please, just leave.

00:34:27.970 --> 00:34:29.320
But martin's got to stay.

00:34:29.520 --> 00:34:30.900
Sorry, can't do that.

00:34:31.230 --> 00:34:32.500
It's not that we like him or anything.

00:34:32.500 --> 00:34:34.830
It's a matter of principle.

00:34:34.830 --> 00:34:36.520
Then I'm sorry, too.

00:34:37.690 --> 00:34:38.520
Walter.

00:34:38.520 --> 00:34:40.670
Walter,
pl-- Don't.

00:35:01.010 --> 00:35:02.410
Sam!

00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:12.750
Come on.

00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:14.060
Come on.

00:35:24.190 --> 00:35:26.080
Come out to the coast.

00:35:39.960 --> 00:35:43.500
We'll get together, have a few laughs.

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:50.000
Oh, man!

00:35:51.590 --> 00:35:52.520
I can't frickin' believe this.

00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:53.530
Ghosts are real.

00:35:53.530 --> 00:35:54.870
What makes you say that?

00:36:05.400 --> 00:36:06.320
But I don't understand.

00:36:06.510 --> 00:36:08.510
How is Walter controlling them?

00:36:08.650 --> 00:36:10.310
Probably that talisman.

00:36:17.580 --> 00:36:18.430
What are you doing?

00:36:18.430 --> 00:36:21.180
If film cameras pick
these suckers up, then...

00:36:21.180 --> 00:36:22.980
Maybe, uh...

00:36:28.400 --> 00:36:29.710
Dean, right there!

00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:36.650
Hey!

00:36:36.650 --> 00:36:37.920
Right there!

00:36:43.360 --> 00:36:43.770
Here.

00:36:43.770 --> 00:36:44.400
Get the idea?

00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:44.870
Yeah.

00:36:44.870 --> 00:36:45.720
All right, you hold them off.

00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:47.210
I'm going after Walter.

00:36:52.190 --> 00:36:53.980
I cannot believe there's an afterlife.

00:36:53.980 --> 00:36:55.720
There's an afterlife, all right.

00:36:55.720 --> 00:36:57.750
But mostly it's a pain in the ass.

00:36:59.480 --> 00:37:00.470
There!

00:37:04.830 --> 00:37:07.790
It's over, Walter.

00:37:11.490 --> 00:37:12.480
TherE.

00:37:12.620 --> 00:37:14.310
Okay, now no one can have it.

00:37:16.840 --> 00:37:18.610
I wouldn't have done that if I were you.

00:37:18.610 --> 00:37:19.860
Yeah?

00:37:19.860 --> 00:37:20.930
Why not?

00:37:21.030 --> 00:37:22.510
'Cause you just freed them.

00:37:23.370 --> 00:37:25.100
We can't stop them now.

00:37:25.540 --> 00:37:27.260
Walter, you brought them back...

00:37:27.990 --> 00:37:29.420
Forced them to murder.

00:37:29.800 --> 00:37:31.760
They're not going to
be very happy with you.

00:37:31.760 --> 00:37:33.090
Yeah?

00:37:33.410 --> 00:37:34.480
So, why not?

00:37:56.170 --> 00:37:59.510
Oh, god.

00:38:01.530 --> 00:38:02.620
There!

00:38:04.280 --> 00:38:05.290
But I don't understand.

00:38:05.570 --> 00:38:07.630
How come the spirits
appear in the camera phone?

00:38:07.630 --> 00:38:10.600
The video must pick up their
frequencies in a way that our eyes can't.

00:38:13.330 --> 00:38:14.730
Oh, God.

00:38:14.850 --> 00:38:15.900
Right there!

00:38:18.460 --> 00:38:19.190
Cut!

00:38:19.190 --> 00:38:20.760
Oh, print that one.

00:38:20.760 --> 00:38:21.990
That's in the movie.

00:38:21.990 --> 00:38:22.630
Oh!

00:38:22.630 --> 00:38:24.220
Loved it, kids,  loved it!

00:38:28.010 --> 00:38:30.920
You find out there's an afterlife,
and this is what you do with it?

00:38:31.980 --> 00:38:33.870
<i>I needed a little jazz on the page.</i>

00:38:53.740 --> 00:38:55.410
You're one hell of a P.A.

00:38:57.080 --> 00:38:58.130
Thank you.

00:39:01.190 --> 00:39:02.180
Hi.

00:39:26.520 --> 00:39:27.890
<i>God, I love this town.</i>

